# Buck2 Android demo app

A Kotlin app with Jetpack Compose, resources, Robolectric and instrumentation
tests, an app bundle and a JNI library, built with the prelude's Android
toolchains. See https://buck2.build/docs/users/languages/android/overview for
the details.

## Requirements

- buck2: https://buck2.build/docs/getting_started/install/
- A JDK. With JDK 17, add `-c java.buck2_java_version=17` to each command.
- The Android SDK, with build tools 35.0.0 and the `android-35` platform, at
  `/opt/android_sdk` or `-c android.sdk_path=<SDK>`.
- For `//app:demoapp_native` and `//app:native_tests`, the Android NDK:
  `-c android.ndk_path=<NDK>`.
- For `buck2 install` and the instrumentation tests, a device or emulator that
  `adb devices` lists.

## Commands

    buck2 build //app:demoapp_debug          # debug APK
    buck2 build //app:demoapp_release        # release APK, shrunk with ProGuard
    buck2 build //app:demoapp_bundle         # app bundle (AAB)
    buck2 install --run //app:demoapp_debug  # install and start the app
    buck2 test //app:tests                   # Robolectric tests, on the JVM
    buck2 test //app:android_tests           # instrumentation tests, on the device
    buck2 test //app:native_tests            # the app with a JNI library, on the device
